Babet 2.9.0 roadmap
====================

[x] Lot A: add configurable babet.spawn() redirections.
[x] Preserve the historical three-pipe default without breaking existing code.
[x] Add inherit, /dev/null, regular-file output and stderr-to-stdout merging.
[x] Add exhaustive validation, lifecycle compatibility tests and rich FR/EN/PDF documentation.
[x] Lot B: add binary-safe native babet.base64.encode()/decode().
[x] Lot C: add generic secure babet.writeFileAtomic().
[x] Lot D: harden worker lifecycle with strict options, status(), join(timeout)
    and cooperative cancellation.
[x] Lot E: add bounded direct worker-to-worker channels after lifecycle rules
    and shared transport primitives are stable.
[x] Perform the final code/tests/docs/PDF/build/release audit.

Deferred ideas retained in notes.md:
- bounded in-memory archive.read() if a concrete use case justifies it;
- parent-side PATH resolution followed by execve;
- forced worker termination (pthread_cancel remains intentionally excluded);
- macOS/BSD portability.
